    "snippet": "---\ntitle: 25 Years of Bestselling Authors and Books\nauthor: Kristen McLean\ndate: 2022-04-19\n---\nBelow, you'll find the 150 bestselling print books in the 2004\u20132021 period, as well as the top-selling authors over the same span as measured by NPD BookScan.\n\nJ.K. Rowling scored the two top-selling titles, with Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows taking the top spot followed by Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince. The bestselling adult title was Fifty Shades of Grey, the first volume in E.L. James's megaselling Fifty Shades series, which was #3 overall on the list.\n\nDespite writing the two most popular print books since 2004, Rowling only finished in third place among bestselling authors. Based on total copies sold, the prolific James Patterson took the top-selling author crown of the past 17 years, followed by another one who was very busy during his lifetime: Dr. Seuss. Jeff Kinney and Nora Roberts rounded out the top five bestselling authors.\n\nTop-Selling Titles, 2004\u20132021\n\n1 Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows\n\nJ.K. Rowling (2007) Scholastic\n\n2 Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince\n\nJ.K. Rowling (2005)\n\nScholastic\n\n3 Fifty Shades of Grey\n\nE.L. James (2012)\n\nVintage\n\n4 Oh, the Places You'll Go!\n\nDr. Seuss (1990)\n\nRandom House\n\n5 Twilight\n\nStephenie Meyer (2006)\n\nLittle, Brown\n\n6 Strengthsfinder 2.0\n\n(2007)\n\nGallup Press\n\n7 Goodnight Moon\n\nMargaret Wise Brown, illus. by Clement Hurd (1991)\n\nHarperFestival\n\n8 The Hunger Games\n\nSuzanne Collins (2010)\n\nScholastic Press\n\n9 The Shack\n\nWilliam P. Young (2008)\n\nWindblown Media\n\n10 The Very Hungry Caterpillar\n\nEric Carle (1994)\n\nPhilomel\n\n11 Breaking Dawn\n\nStephenie Meyer (2008)\n\nLittle, Brown\n\n12 Green Eggs and Ham\n\nDr. Seuss (1960)\n\nRandom House\n\n13 New Moon\n\nStephenie Meyer (2008)\n\nLittle, Brown\n\n14 Brown Bear, Brown Bear, What Do You See? 50th Anniversary Edition\n\nBill Martin Jr., illus. by Eric Carl