    "snippet": "---\ntitle: ThunderCats (2011 TV series) - Wikipedia\ndate: 2011-03-11\n---\ngenre: Action/Adventure, Sword and planet, Superhero\nbased_on: ThunderCats Tobin Wolf\ndeveloper: Ethan Spaulding, Michael Jelenic\nvoices: Will Friedle, Matthew Mercer, Emmanuelle Chriqui, Kevin Michael Richardson, Eamon Pirruccello, Madeleine Hall, Satomi K\u014drogi, Robin Atkin Downes, Clancy Brown, Dee Bradley Baker, Corey Burton, Pamela Adlon\ntheme_music_composer: Kevin KlieschOriginal theme by Bernard Hoffer and Jules Bass.\ncomposer: Kevin Kliesch\ncountry: United StatesJapan\nlanguage: English\nnum_seasons: 1\nnum_episodes: 26\nnetwork: Cartoon Network\nexecutive_producer: Sam Register\nproducer: Michael JelenicEthan Spaulding\neditor: Damon Yoches\ncompany: Warner Bros. Animation\nanimator: Studio 4\u00b0C Thunder Thursdays: ThunderCats Gets (Anime)ted! Fowler Matt June 30, 2011 ign.com September 2, 2012\nruntime: 21\u201322 minutes\nfirst_aired: 29 July 2011\nlast_aired: 16 June 2012\n\nname: ThunderCats (Music from the Warner Bros. Animation Series)\ntype: soundtrack\nartist: Kevin Kleisch\nreleased: October 21, 2012\nlength: 113:51\nlabel: La-La Land Records\nproducer: *Kevin Kleisch, *Dan Goldwasser\n\nThunderCats is a science fantasy animated television series, developed by Ethan Spaulding and Michael Jelenic for Cartoon Network. A reboot of the original 1980s TV series of the same name (which ran from 1985 to 1989), ThunderCats was produced by American studio Warner Bros. Animation and animated by Japanese studio Studio 4\u00b0C, and combined elements of western animation with Japanese anime. The series began with an hour-long premiere on Cartoon Network on July 29, 2011. It is the final animated collaboration of both Arthur Rankin Jr. and Jules Bass, as the former died on January 30, 2014, and the latter died on October 25, 2022.\n\nFollowing the destruction of their home, the kingdom of Thundera, the ThunderCats (a group of humanoid fel"
