    "snippet": "---\ntitle: The Adventures of Hijitus - Wikipedia\ndate: 2014-02-25\n---\nalt_name: Hijitus, Super Hijitus\nnative_name: Las aventuras de Hijitus\ngenre: * Animation, * Comedy, * Adventure\ncreator: Manuel Garc\u00eda Ferr\u00e9\nwriter: * Manuel Garc\u00eda Ferr\u00e9, * In\u00e9s Geldstein, * N\u00e9stor D'Alessandro\ndirector: Manuel Garc\u00eda Ferr\u00e9\nvoices: * N\u00e9stor D'Alessandro, * Pelusa Suero, * Liliana Mamone, * Mario Gian, * Susana Sisto, * Marion Tiffemberg, * Pedro An\u00edbal Mansilla, * Enrique Conlazo\nnarrated: Pedro An\u00edbal Mansilla\ntheme_music_composer: * N\u00e9stor D'Alessandro\ncountry: Argentina\nlanguage: Spanish\nnum_seasons: 8\nnum_episodes: 74 (262 segments) (+ pilot), List of episodes\nproducer: Manuel Garc\u00eda Ferr\u00e9\nruntime: * 1 minute (daily episodes), * 5 minutes (segments), * 5-25 minutes (story arcs)\ncompany: Producciones Garc\u00eda Ferr\u00e9\nnetwork: Canal 13\nfirst_aired: 7 August 1967\nlast_aired: 1 March 1996\n\nThe Adventures of Hijitus () is an Argentine animated series created in 1967 by Spanish cartoonist Manuel Garc\u00eda Ferr\u00e9. It was the first animated series in Latin America that was made for television, and has been considered the most successful series in the history of Latin American cartoons.\n\nThe series first aired on 7 August 1967, on Canal 13, and was rerun throughout the day at different times. It later was compiled into a film format and screened in cinemas.\n\nThe main character of the series is Hijitus, a street child who lives in the sewers of the fictional city of Trulal\u00e1. Trulal\u00e1 is ravaged by the evil actions of villains such as Professor Neurus, Pucho, Granhampa and Dedo Negro, among others. Hijitus is granted magical powers through his hat sombreritus, which allow him to transform himself into Super Hijitus, a strong superhero who can fly. He uses his power to defend his city and his friends: Oaky, Pichichus, Anteojito and Larguirucho.\n\nOrigin