    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Bruja Cachavacha - Wikipedia, la enciclopedia libre\nauthor: Control de autoridades Proyectos Wikimedia Datos Q\ndate: 2008-02-23\n---\n\n\nWikipediaThe free encyclopedia\nSearch Wikipedia\n\nLook for\nDonations\nCreate an account\nAccess\n\nContents disguise\nStart\nCharacteristics\nReferences\nSee also\nWitch Cachavacha\n\nArticle\nDiscussion\nRead\nEdit\nView history\n\nTools\nAppearance disguise\nText\n\nLittle\n\nStandard\n\nBig\nWidth\n\nStandard\n\nBroad\nColor (beta)\n\nAutomatic\n\nClear\n\nDark\nMain article: Hijitus (TV series)\nWitch Cachavacha\nCharacter from Hijitus (series)\nCreated by\tManuel Garc\u00eda Ferr\u00e9\nPerformed by\tN\u00e9stor D'Alessandro , Sebasti\u00e1n Cresp\u00edn (in Soledad and Larguirucho )\nBirth name\tCachavacha\nPhysical characteristics\nRace\tHuman\nSex\tfemale\nFamily and relationships\nSpouse\tSingle woman\nProfessional information\nAllies\tBig bird\nEnemies\tThe rest of Trulala\n[ edit data on Wikidata ]\nThe Witch Cachavacha is an Argentine animated character , aimed at children, created by Manuel Garc\u00eda Ferr\u00e9 and featured in the Hijitus series . She was originally voiced by actor N\u00e9stor D'Alessandro .\n\nShe's about a witch who uses her magic to wreak havoc on the inhabitants of Trulal\u00e1 , in conflict with Hijitus . Cachavacha will take on a life of her own and appear in other fictional works by Garc\u00eda Ferr\u00e9, such as Anteojito and Antifaz .\n\nCharacteristics\nCachavacha lives in the countryside, in a shack. She is constantly accompanied by her faithful talking owl , Pajarraco, who, upon the appearance of Hijitus and his gang, exclaims \"Cachavacha, intruders are approaching!\" and is also her main aide in her mischief, accompanying her on her flying broomstick. Witch Cachavacha rents rooms in her boarding house, and among the food she serves is her famous \"tracatacha candy,\" which causes stomach aches in the boarding house's guests.\n\nIn one episode of the se